duct type. A true result identifies an offer caught by this selected restriction only.","subject":"Breadth of the fee-discount exception"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":1,"root":"node.d9f34661763298a954a3958c","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":1},{"bundle_hash":"88db64f4236b5c6dd4fb98994c83e7f188b4f5718902a9049ae1d3b89bd31fd1","candidate_id":"candidate.ddabc7a87cdf49a6b9332b9395c8c3ea","commitment":"219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c122ef6354d2ef9bf3733e5ed173d1a0cde135f9be","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c1","order":2,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","The general investment-product wording in u14 determines product scope.","Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"}],"distinction":"A defined distributor's non-discount gift promoting a specific investment product outside SFC-authorised funds can be caught. The strongest uncertainty is whether the circular's fund-specific setting limits the otherwise general product wording.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client; actual acceptance or delivery is unnecessary for this offer fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift, assessed before applying the express discount exception; an additional return or incentive is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within u14's exception; merely including a discount elsewhere in a package is insufficient to establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Does paragraph 3.11 confirm the general product scope of this restatement despite the circular's fund-specific subject?"],"statement":"Selected control: general-product gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific investment product or a particular product type is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. This includes promotional linkage to a fund type or fund house. The restriction does not depend on the arrangement being a structured product or on demonstrated distraction.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c1","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"b1e7206d90bf10b3c13a7e255e902ec26c86a733528823b339781758af7129b6","candidate_id":"candidate.faa5572dcf794f7e96cd6f19cfa630fd","commitment":"b2c4cedb4b34e478aa9bf21f84e03eb43726992a4f7b02a5b77b01144f32649d","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.b2c4cedb4b34e478aa9bf21f","order":3,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","The circular's SFC-authorised-fund context limits this selected application of the general wording quoted in u14.","Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns","unit_id":"u15"}],"distinction":"The same distributor's gift promoting only a different investment product is outside this selected application, while gifts connected to SFC-authorised funds remain covered. Outside scope does not mean permitted under the full Code. The strongest uncertainty is that u14 itself states no express SFC-authorised-fund limitation.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client; actual acceptance or delivery is unnecessary for this offer fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift, assessed before applying the express discount exception; an additional return or incentive is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within u14's exception; merely including a discount elsewhere in a package is insufficient to establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection promotion_concerns_authorised_funds)"},"local_id":"reading_2","questions":["Is the fund-specific context a limit on this circular's selected application, or merely the occasion for restating a broader control?"],"statement":"Selected control: fund-context gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such funds is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. Product-type linkage includes relevant funds offered by certain fund houses. Structured-product status and actual distraction are not additional conditions.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.b2c4cedb4b34e478aa9bf21f","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"b1ad6bbab35243fcafd6df8ac7c230787789ab738ce026005aad57af5e6a0d68","candidate_id":"candidate.0eeb944a32594b8dbde075fc5c65867f","commitment":"1ac161f196805b2bf5703abbbc4ab6dcc9335f121ee5427d742080f4355ab4ea","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.1ac161f196805b2bf5703abb","order":4,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one identified promotional offer by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds.","The result is a screen for the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control only, evaluated when scope is true.","Gift, discount and product-link classifications must be supplied from evidence and judgment; unknown classifications remain unknown.","No independent requirement to prove actual investor distraction is added: the text states distraction as the purpose and rationale."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"u15"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"The supported reading attaches the exception to qualifying fee discounts and reaches both individual-product and product-type promotions. For a concrete classification boundary, consider a cash payment after subscribing to funds from one fund house, equal to the subscription fee. If it genuinely reduces that fee, the selected screen passes; if it is a separate gift merely measured by the fee, it fails. The supplied text does not decide which classification applies, so these are unresolved applications rather than two asserted legal rules. By contrast, excluding all fund-house-wide promotions because no single fund is named is contradicted by the express example.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor making the assessed offer is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular’s distributor description.","name":"actor_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer occurs in promoting an investment product or investment service involving such products to a client.","name":"promotion_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion or offered benefit is connected to a specific investment product or particular product type, including a qualifying fund-type or fund-house link.","name":"qualifying_product_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer includes a benefit classified as a gift for paragraph 3.11; a guaranteed return or incentive is not automatically assigned this classification.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the express exception.","name":"qualifying_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(or (not gift_offered) qualifying_fee_discount)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client qualifying_product_link)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Does an after-payment refund legally reduce the relevant fees, or constitute a distinct promotional benefit?","Does the missing FAQ specify how indirect or mixed-product links are assessed?","Are there additional application provisions or exceptions in the complete paragraph 3.11?"],"statement":"For the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control, an in-scope distributor should not offer a gift in a client promotion connected to a specific investment product or particular product type unless the benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges. The linked-product-type explanation carries the same exception. Structured-product classification and section 103 authorisation are separate issues. The strongest unresolved issue is classification of borderline rebates and incentives, which the retained text and absent FAQ do not settle.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: fee-discount exception and product connection"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.1ac161f196805b2bf5703abb","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"262eced0b3bc322fc6df1c64abce614c67198fb6dbaddb85e71c231f55783d24","candidate_id":"candidate.0cfe34359c584b198972a41da6169f08","commitment":"109c6062d36234bb51fb56960254edf7811a619815a11bac22dc51f0d846e9d5","depth":1,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.109c6062d36234bb51fb5696","order":5,"parent":"node.80b94d5df59c55e50b547434","reading":{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one offered benefit in a distributor’s promotion of SFC-authorised funds.","A genuine discount can be treated as excepted even where it otherwise falls within the assessed gift category.","The unqualified words 'fees or charges' do not require those fees to relate to the promoted product.","Unknown facts remain unknown; no missing classification is inferred from the diagnostic label."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"u15"}],"distinction":"Retains the parent’s stronger literal reading: a genuine discount on unrelated service fees is excepted from this selected restriction. In the supplied snapshot, scope is true but the result remains unknown because is_fee_discount is unknown. The DIFFERENT label cannot justify assigning that fact. The hypothesis that a discount exception also clears section 103 fails because u13 and u15 preserve separate controls.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the assessed activity.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered to a client in promotion of a specific fund or particular fund type, including a linkage to funds of certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered and qualifies as a gift before applying the fee-discount exception; an additional return is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit genuinely constitutes a discount of fees or charges, irrespective of which service those fees concern.","name":"is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The fees or charges discounted by the assessed benefit relate to the promoted investment product or product type.","name":"discount_relates_to_promoted_product","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1